WEBVTT

00:11.094 --> 00:12.262
Planet Earth.

00:14.681 --> 00:16.099
I stayed behind.

00:17.226 --> 00:19.478
I said goodbye to Ruby and...

00:19.561 --> 00:21.104
and I stayed.

00:24.483 --> 00:27.819
If I wanted answers
about my sister's disappearance,

00:27.903 --> 00:30.739
I had to find my friend, Henry Thorpe.

00:31.782 --> 00:32.866
Henry.

00:34.284 --> 00:35.911
And finally I did.

00:44.795 --> 00:46.004
You found me.

00:52.761 --> 00:54.388
Henry, you can't leave me.

00:56.223 --> 00:57.891
Yeah. It's too late.

00:58.892 --> 01:00.227
Come on.

01:02.646 --> 01:03.647
No.

01:04.230 --> 01:06.066
I'm sorry you stayed behind.

01:08.735 --> 01:10.237
You wanted me to.

01:12.364 --> 01:13.740
That was before.

01:15.158 --> 01:16.410
Before what?

01:17.619 --> 01:18.620
Your sister.

01:24.293 --> 01:25.836
What did you do to her?

01:26.336 --> 01:27.796
What did you do to her?

01:28.672 --> 01:29.923
Look, I know you know.

01:30.007 --> 01:31.592
You showed me the dress.

01:32.092 --> 01:33.177
You took her.

01:36.180 --> 01:37.181
You took her.

01:43.896 --> 01:44.897
I'm sorry.

01:44.980 --> 01:46.231
I'm sorry.

01:48.817 --> 01:49.985
I'm sorry.

01:50.569 --> 01:51.570
I forgive you.

01:52.070 --> 01:53.530
You just gotta tell me.

01:53.614 --> 01:54.865
You just gotta tell me.

01:56.825 --> 01:57.951
Henry. Henry.

01:58.035 --> 01:59.661
You gotta tell me what happened.

02:00.204 --> 02:02.372
Breathe. Breathe. Breathe.

02:03.498 --> 02:04.499
You just gotta tell me.

02:04.583 --> 02:05.918
What did you do to my sister?

02:06.877 --> 02:08.503
What happened to my sister?

02:38.825 --> 02:40.953
Suicide is unheard of on our planet.

02:42.329 --> 02:43.497
But when we go on mission,

02:45.082 --> 02:47.960
when we stay too long
on worlds not our own, we can...

02:48.710 --> 02:50.546
forget where we come from.

02:51.421 --> 02:52.422
Who we are.

02:54.466 --> 02:57.719
It's rare, but I've seen it before.

03:11.024 --> 03:12.401
Djen's gone.

03:12.985 --> 03:14.069
Really gone.

03:15.237 --> 03:20.200
Any chance I had of solving the mystery
of her disappearance died with Henry.

03:33.964 --> 03:37.009
I was so clear that staying behind
was the right thing to do.

03:38.468 --> 03:45.392
I was so certain that I would uncover
the answers to my loss.

03:49.605 --> 03:53.650
But all I've done is lose more.

03:54.943 --> 03:56.028
My mission,

03:57.196 --> 03:58.488
my friends,

04:00.240 --> 04:01.325
my home.

04:05.954 --> 04:06.997
And so...

04:09.333 --> 04:10.375
now I'm alone.

04:13.837 --> 04:14.838
Here.

04:15.380 --> 04:18.382
Good morning, my friend.

04:24.264 --> 04:25.891
I can never go back home.

04:27.351 --> 04:28.352
But...

04:29.061 --> 04:30.521
there's always California.

04:37.945 --> 04:38.987
Dear, John.

04:39.738 --> 04:43.367
If you're reading this, it means you
didn't listen and decided to stay behind.

04:45.619 --> 04:46.620
As your friend,

04:46.703 --> 04:50.582
the thought of not seeing you again
is more painful than I can put into words.

04:51.124 --> 04:52.626
But I do understand.

04:53.585 --> 04:59.132
Of all the planets I ever visited,
Earth was the hardest to leave.

04:59.758 --> 05:04.680
The colors, the noises,
the winter clouds over Santa Monica.

05:05.180 --> 05:10.102
This place, for better or worse,
takes ahold of you.

05:19.027 --> 05:21.071
You'll have to find a way
to enjoy it on your own,

05:22.406 --> 05:24.032
because I have to go now.

05:26.326 --> 05:30.205
Be strong, be good, be safe.

05:32.583 --> 05:33.709
I love you.

05:34.376 --> 05:35.377
Ruby.

05:55.647 --> 05:57.524
Mr. Sugar. Your mail.

05:59.902 --> 06:01.737
- Welcome back.
- Thank you, Elinor.

06:04.198 --> 06:05.199
Thanks.

06:09.286 --> 06:14.625
PS, I renewed your subscription
to American Cinematographer, just in case.

07:21.275 --> 07:24.069
All right,
no one else can know about this.

07:24.152 --> 07:26.113
Do you understand? It's against the rules.

07:26.655 --> 07:28.782
I'm trusting
you all know how to keep a secret.

07:29.825 --> 07:30.826
Okay?

07:48.260 --> 07:51.221
Come! Frida, Ben!

07:51.305 --> 07:52.598
Frida, Ben!

07:52.681 --> 07:54.641
Let's go! Let's go, buddy!

07:59.104 --> 08:00.355
Ruby,

08:00.856 --> 08:03.442
I do love my American Cinematographer
subscription.

08:03.525 --> 08:05.027
So there's some good news.

08:10.657 --> 08:14.411
Still, at this point I was hoping
things would get a bit busier.

08:16.914 --> 08:21.793
Find a client, take on a new case,
take my mind off things.

08:23.420 --> 08:24.671
It's not as easy as I thought.

08:28.091 --> 08:31.094
Ruby did a lot more for me
than renew magazine subscriptions,

08:31.178 --> 08:34.056
she handled the business side of things.

08:36.015 --> 08:37.601
Not many people have my number.

08:39.436 --> 08:43.023
And so it was a nice surprise
when I got a call from an old friend.

08:44.691 --> 08:45.817
Munzer!

08:47.361 --> 08:48.445
Munzer Amin...

08:49.029 --> 08:50.906
The limo driver with the sick daughter.

08:51.490 --> 08:52.658
Fatemeh is all better now,

08:52.741 --> 08:55.285
but he asked if I might meet
with someone who could use some help.

08:55.369 --> 08:58.872
I believe in you, Danny.
Go out there and kick his fucking ass.

09:01.208 --> 09:02.459
Danny Moon.

09:08.924 --> 09:11.093
A hope to be up-and-comer from Korea.

09:14.555 --> 09:16.640
Danny's an immigrant. Like me.

09:17.349 --> 09:19.560
Like most people
in this part of Los Angeles.

09:20.769 --> 09:22.688
Munzer knew him from the neighborhood.

09:23.438 --> 09:24.690
Follow through!

09:25.440 --> 09:26.900
He said he was a good kid.

09:32.197 --> 09:33.031
Tough kid.

09:33.699 --> 09:34.575
Real tough.

09:35.701 --> 09:38.954
And the winner by unanimous decision...

09:39.454 --> 09:42.749
Danny Moon!

09:46.879 --> 09:48.839
A young man with a temper
who is good at fighting

09:48.922 --> 09:50.549
seems like a dangerous concoction,

09:51.550 --> 09:53.844
but maybe
it just goes with the job description.

09:55.345 --> 09:57.222
Still, if Danny's the good Moon brother,

09:57.306 --> 10:00.100
I was curious to hear
about the one that's trouble.

10:01.768 --> 10:04.188
His brother Ji Moon has gone missing.

10:04.271 --> 10:05.689
And that was three days ago?

10:05.772 --> 10:07.232
- Nothing since?
- No.

10:07.316 --> 10:09.484
You guys, you usually talk every day?

10:10.360 --> 10:11.653
We live together.

10:11.737 --> 10:13.739
Yeah, but if you're two ships passing...

10:13.822 --> 10:15.199
We're not two ships.

10:16.992 --> 10:18.577
I mean he's a fuck-up.

10:18.660 --> 10:20.996
He's high lately pretty much always.

10:22.998 --> 10:24.166
I don't know, man.

10:24.249 --> 10:27.211
I think this is just him being stupid,
trying to scare me.

10:28.462 --> 10:29.463
Don't you?

10:34.343 --> 10:35.511
Play them again.

10:58.909 --> 10:59.910
Shit.

11:01.119 --> 11:02.246
Play the other one.

11:07.501 --> 11:08.544
Okay.

11:08.627 --> 11:09.628
Okay.

11:11.046 --> 11:13.799
Okay. Okay, I got away. For now.

11:13.882 --> 11:15.050
I think I'm safe for now.

11:15.634 --> 11:16.969
Oh, my God, bro.

11:17.636 --> 11:19.221
What I just saw.

11:19.304 --> 11:20.681
I saw this fucking...

11:21.348 --> 11:23.350
He fucking looked down
on me with those fucking eyes,

11:23.433 --> 11:24.768
and he said, "Run."

11:24.852 --> 11:26.812
Then he let me go,
so I just fucking ran, bro.

11:26.895 --> 11:28.272
I ran like hell.

11:29.940 --> 11:31.233
But he'll be coming. I know it.

11:31.316 --> 11:32.776
He's gonna fucking come for me.

11:33.735 --> 11:35.112
He'll be looking for me.

11:36.196 --> 11:37.698
I'm scared, bro.

11:38.866 --> 11:39.992
But I'll be all right.

11:40.784 --> 11:42.077
I'll come up with a plan.

11:43.453 --> 11:44.872
But no cops, okay?

11:44.955 --> 11:48.959
Whatever you do, don't call the cops.
Don't call the fucking cops. Shit.

11:51.503 --> 11:52.629
Just keep working.

11:53.881 --> 11:55.549
Just keep training like I taught you.

11:55.632 --> 11:58.385
Two rounds, shadow box.
Two rounds, double-end bag.

11:58.886 --> 12:00.220
He's high obviously.

12:00.721 --> 12:02.014
Stressed out, seeing things.

12:02.097 --> 12:04.016
But the fear in his voice...

12:04.641 --> 12:05.642
well, that's real.

12:05.726 --> 12:08.312
Don't forget your footwork.
'Cause that's your best weapon, okay?

12:11.565 --> 12:12.608
I know.

12:12.691 --> 12:14.318
A missing sibling in trouble.

12:14.985 --> 12:16.278
Ruby would disapprove.

12:17.154 --> 12:18.530
"Bit on the nose, Sugar."

12:19.823 --> 12:21.158
And she'd tell me to move on.

12:21.241 --> 12:22.367
I love you, bro.

12:23.660 --> 12:24.828
Don't give up on me.

12:26.830 --> 12:30.626
But if I walk away, who helps them?

12:34.171 --> 12:35.964
No. No, this is it.

12:37.216 --> 12:38.967
This is the case I take.

12:41.762 --> 12:44.389
Danny gave me a list
of his brother's usual hangouts.

12:44.890 --> 12:47.434
It was already late
but I wanted to get started.

12:47.976 --> 12:49.269
And besides,

12:50.395 --> 12:52.397
while the rest of LA is climbing into bed,

12:53.941 --> 12:55.692
Koreatown is just getting going.

13:05.827 --> 13:07.704
Hey, can I talk to your boss?

13:13.001 --> 13:14.670
You seen this guy? Ji Moon.

13:27.516 --> 13:29.601
Come on! Come on, get him!

13:44.157 --> 13:46.285
Hey, have you seen
this guy around? Ji Moon?

13:49.663 --> 13:52.583
Hey, guys. Looking for someone. Ji Moon?

13:52.666 --> 13:54.751
His brother said he comes here sometimes.

13:54.835 --> 13:55.836
No?

14:10.058 --> 14:11.768
So the one with the eight in it
goes in last?

14:13.103 --> 14:14.104
Hey, mister.

14:15.439 --> 14:16.815
That your car?

14:16.899 --> 14:19.359
Silver blue '66 Corvette Stingray.

14:20.569 --> 14:24.656
300 horsepower variant with
a two-speed Powerglide transmission.

14:24.740 --> 14:25.866
She's a beauty, huh?

14:28.076 --> 14:30.829
Hey. One game? You and me?

14:32.080 --> 14:34.208
I win,
you tell me something about Ji Moon.

14:35.042 --> 14:37.920
You win, you take her for a spin.

14:39.630 --> 14:40.964
What do you say?

14:53.519 --> 14:54.520
Does... Does that count?

14:55.771 --> 14:56.980
Nah, man. Do-over.

14:57.064 --> 14:59.149
Thank you.

15:37.396 --> 15:38.689
All right.

15:41.024 --> 15:42.317
Ji Moon.

15:42.401 --> 15:43.777
Hey, mister.

15:43.861 --> 15:45.070
They took your car.

15:54.204 --> 15:55.455
Come on.

15:55.539 --> 15:57.040
Someone took your car.

15:57.916 --> 15:59.126
Yeah.

16:02.588 --> 16:03.797
I saw who did it.

16:04.882 --> 16:06.884
Total asshole but he's a friend of mine.

16:08.010 --> 16:09.887
Do you want me
to try and see if I can find him?

16:09.970 --> 16:11.346
Maybe I can get it back for you.

16:12.014 --> 16:13.724
- Yes please.
- Okay.

16:15.058 --> 16:16.310
300 bucks?

16:20.355 --> 16:21.523
500?

16:22.774 --> 16:25.110
300. I just got a credit card.

16:26.695 --> 16:28.572
No problem, I have a card reader.

16:28.655 --> 16:29.656
Well, that's lucky.

16:32.492 --> 16:33.493
Nice.

16:34.536 --> 16:35.913
So what do you do for work?

16:36.496 --> 16:37.873
I'm a private investigator.

16:38.707 --> 16:40.000
Okay, for like divorces?

16:40.083 --> 16:42.336
Like... husbands and hookers kind of stuff?

16:42.419 --> 16:44.338
No, no divorces. Missing persons.

16:46.256 --> 16:47.466
Cool.

16:49.301 --> 16:51.178
- Okay, I'll be right back.
- All right.

16:58.393 --> 17:00.479
Where did you learn
to shoot pool like that?

17:02.147 --> 17:04.148
Movies. Mostly.

17:14.535 --> 17:15.661
You're worried about him.

17:18.163 --> 17:19.540
Hannah McDaniels.

17:20.082 --> 17:21.458
Girl I heard he was seeing.

17:21.959 --> 17:23.669
Hannah McDaniels. Okay.

17:23.752 --> 17:25.420
She's a doctor or something.

17:26.797 --> 17:28.006
So, why are you worried?

17:30.759 --> 17:32.094
'Cause it's fucking Ji.

17:33.178 --> 17:36.431
And this time
a lot of people are looking for him.

17:37.140 --> 17:38.141
Like who?

17:42.771 --> 17:46.400
Let's just say some guys
who don't wear suits and ties.

17:47.484 --> 17:49.069
I hope you find him first.

17:50.237 --> 17:52.197
You really think
she's coming back with the car?

18:05.043 --> 18:06.128
I miss my dog.

18:11.758 --> 18:13.343
I miss my friends.

18:24.354 --> 18:26.690
Is she actually not coming back
with my car?

18:34.281 --> 18:35.282
Shit, look.

18:35.991 --> 18:36.992
It's your lucky day.

18:53.383 --> 18:55.135
Could tell you a lot

18:56.303 --> 19:00.807
But you've got to be true to your code

19:02.643 --> 19:05.312
Make it one for my baby

19:05.395 --> 19:09.233
And one more for the road

19:29.586 --> 19:31.505
Maybe someone else stayed behind.

19:40.389 --> 19:42.933
Second group, third wave, California.

19:43.517 --> 19:44.601
John Sugar.

19:46.687 --> 19:48.897
I'm still here if anyone else is.

19:51.108 --> 19:52.109
It'd be...

19:54.903 --> 19:56.613
It'd be nice to talk to someone.

20:14.715 --> 20:16.592
Outgoing message sent.

20:22.723 --> 20:25.309
I tend to keep to myself
when I'm not on the clock.

20:30.939 --> 20:32.941
Order in, watch a movie.

20:34.860 --> 20:36.570
But I've been on my own for months now.

20:38.363 --> 20:40.949
A night on the town might do me some good.

20:42.117 --> 20:43.577
It's quarter to three

20:44.953 --> 20:47.539
There's no one in the place

20:48.957 --> 20:50.667
Except you and me

20:50.751 --> 20:54.004
Not that the hotel restaurant
counts as a night on the town but,

20:54.087 --> 20:55.881
you know... baby steps.

20:55.964 --> 20:57.925
So set 'em up, Joe

20:59.510 --> 21:01.637
I got a little story

21:03.388 --> 21:06.016
I think you should know

21:10.395 --> 21:12.606
We're drinkin', my friend...

21:12.689 --> 21:14.483
- No cinnamon?
- No cinnamon.

21:14.566 --> 21:15.901
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

21:15.984 --> 21:20.614
...to the end of a brief episode

21:24.826 --> 21:28.914
Make it one for my baby

21:31.083 --> 21:34.503
And one more for the road

21:41.426 --> 21:43.971
I got the routine...

22:01.613 --> 22:04.324
Outside of the movies,
the boxing world is pretty new to me.

22:06.618 --> 22:08.412
I learn as I go but...

22:13.500 --> 22:16.628
it's already clear that these brothers
have been going in different directions.

22:18.255 --> 22:19.256
Danny on the rise.

22:20.382 --> 22:21.341
Ji struggling.

22:21.842 --> 22:22.926
Going the other way.

22:24.761 --> 22:28.682
Still, Ji sounded like he was more
than just struggling on that phone call.

22:31.476 --> 22:32.811
He sounded terrified.

23:04.801 --> 23:07.221
I tracked down the name
I got at the pool hall.

23:07.304 --> 23:11.058
Ji's friend Hannah McDaniels,
she's a nurse at St. Anthony's.

23:11.808 --> 23:13.227
Maybe she knows something.

23:13.769 --> 23:14.978
Sign in at the front desk.

23:15.062 --> 23:16.271
Sure.

23:17.481 --> 23:18.982
Blaine. That's a cool name.

23:19.566 --> 23:20.567
Right.

23:20.651 --> 23:21.902
What, you don't like it?

23:22.528 --> 23:25.822
Come on, man, I've been getting shit
for Blaine ever since I could even talk.

23:25.906 --> 23:28.534
That's Bogart's character in Casablanca.

23:29.451 --> 23:32.162
Never saw it,
but that's my mom's favorite movie.

23:32.246 --> 23:33.664
Well, he's tough, he's smart,

23:33.747 --> 23:36.583
and in the end he sacrifices
his own interests for a greater cause.

23:36.667 --> 23:38.168
I mean, you should see it. You would...

23:38.252 --> 23:39.419
You'd thank your mom.

23:39.503 --> 23:40.796
Yeah, Blaine's a hero.

23:42.339 --> 23:44.383
- John Sugar.
- Blaine Bosco.

23:44.967 --> 23:46.051
Very cool.

23:52.599 --> 23:55.143
Excuse me?
I'm looking for Hannah McDaniels.

23:55.227 --> 23:56.478
Yes?

23:56.562 --> 23:57.604
Hey.

23:59.106 --> 24:01.650
I wanna ask you a couple
of questions about Ji Moon.

24:02.234 --> 24:03.360
What?

24:03.443 --> 24:05.070
- Ji Moon. I was told--
- No.

24:06.238 --> 24:08.073
I don't know that. No idea.

24:08.782 --> 24:10.242
You don't know what?

24:11.618 --> 24:12.786
She's nervous.

24:14.496 --> 24:15.789
Hiding something.

24:17.374 --> 24:18.834
So I'm getting fired now?

24:20.294 --> 24:21.295
Because of this?

24:23.797 --> 24:25.632
Might be good
if we went somewhere to talk.

24:26.133 --> 24:27.342
Privately.

24:27.843 --> 24:30.053
You scared the shit out of me.
I thought you were HR.

24:30.137 --> 24:32.890
No. I'm sorry, I didn't mean to scare you.

24:33.390 --> 24:34.892
So, Ji.

24:35.934 --> 24:37.186
You know where I could find him?

24:37.769 --> 24:38.812
No.

24:38.896 --> 24:40.856
Can you tell me a little bit about him?

24:41.732 --> 24:44.568
I mean, if you're not HR,
and you're not police,

24:44.651 --> 24:46.069
I don't really have to, do I?

24:46.153 --> 24:47.571
No. No, you don't have to.

24:48.447 --> 24:50.324
You know,
if you care about your boyfriend--

24:50.407 --> 24:51.617
Boyfriend?

24:51.700 --> 24:53.577
Ji is not my boyfriend.

24:53.660 --> 24:55.454
Is he someone you care about?

24:57.831 --> 24:59.208
He's all right.

24:59.291 --> 25:02.753
Well, I think there's a chance
he might be in a bit of trouble.

25:04.796 --> 25:05.923
Yeah? Like what?

25:06.590 --> 25:07.591
I'm not sure yet.

25:08.800 --> 25:09.801
But...

25:10.302 --> 25:11.803
That's why I'm asking for your help.

25:26.235 --> 25:28.278
He was here four days ago.

25:28.362 --> 25:29.738
Here in the hospital?

25:31.156 --> 25:32.157
Doing what?

25:34.159 --> 25:35.619
Okay.

25:36.537 --> 25:39.540
But you gotta understand
this was his idea.

25:49.716 --> 25:52.553
It was a graveyard shift,
so it was just a few of us working.

25:54.263 --> 25:55.347
Hey, Stace.

25:55.848 --> 25:57.808
- Hey, Hannah.
- Where's Luann?

25:57.891 --> 25:59.476
Maltby in 411.

25:59.560 --> 26:01.228
- Bedpan.
- Lucky her.

26:01.854 --> 26:02.855
How you holding up?

26:04.189 --> 26:05.691
It's been one of those nights.

26:09.403 --> 26:10.946
Something's up with the printer.

26:11.446 --> 26:12.447
Let me see.

26:12.531 --> 26:14.700
I mean, I pressed print like I always do.

26:14.783 --> 26:16.159
Maybe it's the Wi-Fi.

26:17.828 --> 26:19.246
Here, let me try it again.

26:21.748 --> 26:24.042
Should be fine. It's brand-new.

26:25.502 --> 26:27.337
So typical of this place.

26:28.714 --> 26:30.340
I'd rather have the bedpan than this.

26:33.010 --> 26:34.428
Okay, how's it--

26:34.511 --> 26:36.430
Finally! Thanks, Stace.

26:37.306 --> 26:38.307
Yeah.

26:38.807 --> 26:40.809
- All right, I gotta go do rounds.
- Okay.

26:41.894 --> 26:44.188
Ji only needed a minute.

27:02.581 --> 27:05.417
We were supposed to
meet up after but he never showed.

27:09.463 --> 27:12.758
He probably just kept the drugs for
himself and is off somewhere having fun.

27:13.967 --> 27:14.968
Maybe.

27:15.052 --> 27:16.929
No, like, definitely, he is.

27:17.513 --> 27:20.766
He's a wild man. I mean,
who even said he was my boyfriend?

27:21.475 --> 27:23.018
I guess they were confused.

27:23.644 --> 27:25.103
Let me know if you hear from him.

27:25.187 --> 27:26.188
Yeah.

27:26.688 --> 27:28.398
Oh, this stairwell,
where you last saw him,

27:28.482 --> 27:29.483
where is it?

27:51.088 --> 27:52.047
Shit.

28:00.681 --> 28:03.058
A wild man with a thermos full of drugs.

28:04.726 --> 28:07.354
For someone like Ji,
that can get you in a lot of trouble.

28:10.691 --> 28:12.150
I looked all over.

28:13.443 --> 28:16.238
The underground clubs, the bars,
the dealer courts.

28:18.365 --> 28:19.491
I ended up here.

28:22.244 --> 28:23.704
Three minutes, they say.

28:24.413 --> 28:27.291
After an overdose, you've got
three minutes for help to arrive.

28:28.000 --> 28:30.502
Get revived and come back from the dead.

28:34.798 --> 28:38.093
This poor guy. His help came too late.

28:38.719 --> 28:40.095
I'm sorry.

28:41.513 --> 28:42.514
I'm glad it wasn't Ji.

28:42.598 --> 28:44.141
But if he keeps pushing his luck...

28:48.896 --> 28:51.440
the next time it'll be him
they drive off into the night.

29:16.965 --> 29:18.091
Hello.

29:18.175 --> 29:19.176
Hi.

29:23.263 --> 29:26.058
I don't mean it as... Have we met before?

29:28.936 --> 29:29.937
I don't think so.

29:30.020 --> 29:33.190
Zurich, the sustainability conference.
That wasn't you?

29:33.273 --> 29:34.566
No. No.

29:35.359 --> 29:36.944
- My mistake.
- Not at all.

29:38.278 --> 29:39.488
John Sugar.

29:39.571 --> 29:42.366
Sugar. Like what, sweet?

29:44.868 --> 29:45.869
I suppose.

29:47.204 --> 29:48.205
I'm Charlotte.

29:49.581 --> 29:50.832
Like the web?

29:50.916 --> 29:52.918
Like the spider's web.

29:56.421 --> 29:57.422
I got to, uh...

29:59.132 --> 30:00.634
Nice to meet you, Charlotte.

30:00.717 --> 30:02.135
You too, John Sugar.

30:03.595 --> 30:04.763
Good night.

30:13.814 --> 30:15.941
I'd been waiting for that text to come in.

30:16.775 --> 30:19.319
The Moon brothers are my priority, but...

30:21.321 --> 30:23.615
I've got something else going on the side.

30:26.243 --> 30:27.452
Something personal.

30:40.674 --> 30:41.675
This is it.

30:42.593 --> 30:43.635
The Hollywood Hills.

30:45.512 --> 30:48.932
The real estate broker told me
that Bogart used to live right nearby.

30:52.102 --> 30:54.438
- Sight unseen.
- Yeah, I trust you.

30:56.356 --> 30:57.357
All set.

30:57.900 --> 30:58.901
Great.

30:58.984 --> 31:00.736
And the S.P.A.C.E. people
will contact you directly?

31:01.737 --> 31:02.738
That's right.

31:02.821 --> 31:04.865
- I hope you like it.
- I'm sure I will.

31:04.948 --> 31:06.033
- Thank you.
- Pleasure.

31:34.811 --> 31:36.688
Well, at least my stuff arrived.

31:50.077 --> 31:53.914
In LA, a three-bedroom
with a dirty swimming pool isn't cheap.

31:55.624 --> 31:58.669
But I'm not complaining about the view.

32:05.926 --> 32:07.302
My people were betrayed.

32:07.928 --> 32:09.888
Hunted and forced to flee the planet.

32:10.597 --> 32:11.807
Why?

32:13.058 --> 32:14.184
That's my question.

32:19.523 --> 32:22.568
The home of Senator Tyson Pavich.

32:23.318 --> 32:24.862
Father of Ryan.

32:25.863 --> 32:27.489
Stop!

32:29.616 --> 32:31.785
The son died of his sins.

32:33.287 --> 32:35.789
But I'm thinking
the father has secrets of his own.

32:36.915 --> 32:38.375
They found out about us...

32:39.793 --> 32:42.087
- the humans.
- Yes. Some did.

32:43.755 --> 32:45.465
These are powerful people.

32:45.549 --> 32:46.592
I'm sure.

32:47.134 --> 32:49.595
They can exterminate us
at any time if they want to.

32:49.678 --> 32:52.306
How did we-- How did they
find out about us?

32:52.389 --> 32:55.225
I don't know that part.
And at this point, does it even matter?

32:55.309 --> 32:56.560
Of course it matters.

32:58.145 --> 32:59.605
More than anything.

33:01.732 --> 33:03.775
Six months later and it still matters.

33:07.070 --> 33:08.113
I'm still here.

33:10.532 --> 33:13.410
Asking questions, looking for answers.

33:15.495 --> 33:16.496
Only now...

33:17.789 --> 33:19.416
there's no one left to stop me.

33:20.167 --> 33:22.544
You do that for a couple
of rounds, make it look good.

33:22.628 --> 33:23.629
Make a good showing.

33:23.712 --> 33:25.714
And the first time he connects,
and you feel hurt,

33:25.797 --> 33:27.883
stay down till the referee counts you out.

33:27.966 --> 33:30.552
I don't know.
What will people think of me?

33:30.636 --> 33:32.596
What do you care
what a bunch of bloodthirsty,

33:32.679 --> 33:33.972
screaming people think of you?

33:34.056 --> 33:35.891
Did you ever get a look at their faces?

33:35.974 --> 33:38.268
They pay a few lousy bucks
hoping to see a man get killed.

33:38.352 --> 33:39.686
To hell with them!

33:39.770 --> 33:41.939
Get your money and get
out of this rotten business.

33:42.022 --> 33:45.484
I know, I know. Two cases at once.

33:45.567 --> 33:48.904
It's a lot to take on but I'll make time.

34:13.387 --> 34:14.471
Shit--

34:41.623 --> 34:44.626
In this world, doing this job...

34:45.127 --> 34:46.545
Shit.

34:48.255 --> 34:50.507
...someone always ends up getting hurt.

34:53.844 --> 34:56.263
Sometimes it's the other guy going down...

34:59.099 --> 35:01.935
but sometimes it's you.

35:05.439 --> 35:07.149
You or the people that you love.

35:17.951 --> 35:19.494
Ruby was right.

35:19.578 --> 35:20.913
What she said in her letter

35:21.705 --> 35:23.707
about having to find a way
to be on my own here.

35:24.541 --> 35:26.418
In this place, with these people.

35:27.836 --> 35:29.421
So I gotta be careful.

35:30.005 --> 35:31.298
It's just me now.

35:32.508 --> 35:33.800
I have to be strong.

35:33.884 --> 35:35.135
Be good.

35:35.636 --> 35:37.429
I have to stay busy or else...

35:38.514 --> 35:40.015
I could end up like Henry.

35:41.767 --> 35:43.185
Losing my mind too.
